NOT CURRENTLY A DEPENDENCY, AND NO CODE FROM IT IS PRESENT IN THIS TREE.

dom_smoothie 0.18.0 was read as prior art while deciding whether to build this engine at
all; that analysis is docs/adr/0001-probe-b-dom-smoothie.md. Reading is not copying, so
this section confers no attribution obligation today. It is recorded here in advance
because two planned uses would create one, and the obligation is easier to honour if it is
written down before the code lands than remembered afterwards:

  1. Transcription. `legibility-legacy` will port Readability.js's scoring arithmetic, word
     lists, comma table, title-separator table, metadata key tables and URL helpers into
     Rust. Where that work is informed by dom_smoothie's existing transcription of the same
     upstream algorithm, the file gets an attribution header naming the dom_smoothie source
     file, and this section is rewritten in the present tense.

  2. Test-only dependency. dom_smoothie is planned as a second differential baseline in the
     parity harness -- an observation point, not an authority, with its deliberate
     divergences from Readability.js registered as expected divergences rather than
     failures. The most consequential is `min_score_to_adjust` (default 5.0), which causes
     candidates scoring at or below 5.0 to skip link-density normalization entirely.

Neither has happened yet. When either does, this notice must be updated in the same commit.

